@suds\_singh Thank you so much for your support!!

Adana Marukhyan

@ankurmodi Just signed up for OpenMarket and started exploring =)

Congrats on the launch - it's really good one! [...] Why it got personal  
Cosmo, my 3 year-old golden retriever, had repeated bouts of suspected -pancreatitis, caused by poor quality food from a brand everybody knows. It is painful, it can turn serious quickly, and once a dog has had it, what you feed him is most of how you stop it coming back. We were told to move him onto natural food.  

I found five products. Every one of them said natural, low fat and vet formulated. There was no honest way to tell them apart, so I chose the best packaging, which means I chose the best marketer. I got it wrong, and Cosmo could not tell me it was not working.  

I had every advantage and I still could not check a claim on a bag of dog food, for a decision that genuinely mattered. I am sure I am not the only person who has felt that way. [...] Priya K

@ankurmodi a story about his dog's food is exactly why ecommerce feels so broken right now.,glad someone is finally tackling this.

Tiwaysyya Segaran

@ankurmodi  @priya\_kushwaha1 Completely agree! This is a mission that is personal to us and we're so happy that others feel the same way.

Dipanshu Kushwaha

@david\_mataciunas  @ankurmodi what happens when two AI agents disagree on whether a claim is actually proven ?

David Mataciunas

@ankurmodi  @dipanshu\_kushwaha5 That’s where our referee agent comes in. It checks the underlying evidence, reviews, and third-party sources, then decides how strong the claim actually is. If the evidence is weak or conflicting, the claim gets downgraded rather than treated as fact.

Csaba Kissi
